---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Lunch rush: who delivers what" hint="The same 30-minute lunch rush on a city grid is run three times: nearest courier at once, two orders per courier, and a window that assigns couriers to orders together. Change the number of couriers and see which one wins.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>With the default <b>100 orders and 20 couriers</b> (Monday), couriers are short. <b>Nearest courier</b> sends a courier the moment an order arrives, so couriers stand at counters while the rest of the orders queue: <b>34.5 minutes</b> per order and 14.3 minutes of food waiting. <b>Two per courier</b> (27.4 min) and the <b>window</b> (29.1 min) are much better, because they save courier time in different ways.</li>
    <li>Raise couriers to <b>40</b>: queues vanish and only <b>timing</b> matters. The window sends couriers so that they arrive when the food is ready, so it wins with <b>20.3 minutes</b> and 0.1 minutes of food waiting. Pairing (21.8 min) is now slightly worse than nearest courier (21.4 min), because the first order's food sits while the second is collected.</li>
    <li>Drop couriers to <b>12</b>: everything slows (59.0, 40.8 and 46.3 minutes) but <b>pairing</b> degrades least, since it carries two orders per trip, and the window beats nearest courier by 13 minutes. No single method is best at every level of supply, which is why real platforms switch between them.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg fdb" data-fdb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Orders in the 30-minute rush <input type="range" min="40" max="160" step="10" value="100" data-o /> <b data-oval></b></label>
      <label>Couriers <input type="range" min="8" max="40" value="20" data-c /> <b data-cval></b></label>
      <label>Window or longest wait for a partner (minutes) <input type="range" min="1" max="6" value="3" data-w /> <b data-wval></b></label>
      <label>Lunch day <select class="pg-in" data-seed>
        <option value="7">Monday</option>
        <option value="19">Tuesday</option>
        <option value="31">Wednesday</option>
      </select></label>
    </div>
    <svg class="fd-map" viewBox="0 0 240 240" role="img" aria-label="City grid: squares are restaurants, dots are the starting couriers, small crosses are customers" data-map></svg>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Nearest courier, at once</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Two orders per courier</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Window with global assignment</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: a 24 by 24 grid and a courier covers 2 cells a minute. Orders are placed during 30 minutes from 12 restaurants in three clusters, the food is ready 9 to 17 minutes after the order, and every number is the average over all orders. <b>Food waiting</b> is the time from the food being ready to the courier leaving the last pickup. <b>Utilisation</b> is the share of the time that couriers spend moving, until the last delivery. Nearest courier uses only idle couriers and serves orders in the order they arrived. Two per courier pairs orders from restaurants at most 4 cells apart and customers at most 8 apart, and an unpaired order waits up to the chosen number of minutes for a partner. The window decides every few minutes, only for orders that are due, which means the food is ready within the window plus 4 minutes. It matches orders to couriers (also couriers who are finishing a trip) with the Hungarian algorithm, using the cost of cold food, courier waiting and distance.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query } from '../../playground';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-fdb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    // ---- simulation (pure functions; the page only calls them) ----
    //#sim-start
    const G = 24; const SPEED = 2;
    const RESTAURANTS = 12; const REST_SPREAD = 5; // restaurants sit within +-2 cells of a centre
    const ORDER_WINDOW_MIN = 30; const PREP = { min: 9, range: 9 }; // orders arrive over 30 min; food takes 9 to 17 min
    const FAR = 1e9; // larger than any distance
    const HORIZON_MIN = 400; // stop simulating after this
    const BATCH = { restMax: 4, custMax: 8 }; // two orders share a courier when restaurants and customers are this close
    const LOOKAHEAD_MIN = 4; // window assignment also plans orders ready up to 4 min after the next window
    const UNAVAILABLE = 1e6; // cost for a courier who is busy past the window
    const WEIGHTS = { foodWait: 1.5, drive: 0.5, busy: 0.5 }; // window cost: food waiting counts 1.5x, courier waiting 1x
    const MAP_PX = 240;
    const WORSE_X = 1.25; // 25% slower than the best is bad
    const PLENTIFUL = 0.3; // couriers per order above which couriers are plentiful
    type P = { x: number; y: number };
    type O = { id: number; placed: number; rest: P; cust: P; ready: number };
    type C = { pos: P; free: number; moving: number; wait: number };
    type S = { deliv: number; food: number; n: number; end: number };
    const dist = (a: P, b: P) => Math.abs(a.x - b.x) + Math.abs(a.y - b.y);
    const tt = (a: P, b: P) => dist(a, b) / SPEED;
    function makeWorld(seed0: number, nOrders: number, nCouriers: number) {
      // Numerical Recipes LCG
      let seed = seed0; const rnd = () => ((seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
      const centres = [{ x: 5, y: 6 }, { x: 17, y: 8 }, { x: 11, y: 18 }];
      const clamp = (v: number) => Math.max(0, Math.min(G - 1, v));
      const rests: P[] = Array.from({ length: RESTAURANTS }, (_, i) => { const c = centres[i % centres.length]; return { x: clamp(c.x + Math.floor(rnd() * REST_SPREAD) - 2), y: clamp(c.y + Math.floor(rnd() * REST_SPREAD) - 2) }; });
      const orders: O[] = Array.from({ length: nOrders }, (_, id) => {
        const placed = Math.floor(rnd() * ORDER_WINDOW_MIN); const rest = rests[Math.floor(rnd() * rests.length)];
        return { id, placed, rest, cust: { x: Math.floor(rnd() * G), y: Math.floor(rnd() * G) }, ready: placed + PREP.min + Math.floor(rnd() * PREP.range) };
      }).sort((a, b) => a.placed - b.placed || a.id - b.id);
      const couriers: C[] = Array.from({ length: nCouriers }, () => ({ pos: { x: Math.floor(rnd() * G), y: Math.floor(rnd() * G) }, free: 0, moving: 0, wait: 0 }));
      return { rests, orders, couriers };
    }
    // Plan one trip for a courier carrying one or two orders; tries both pickup orders and both drop orders.
    function trip(c: C, t: number, os: O[]) {
      const start = Math.max(c.free, t); let best: any = null;
      const perms = os.length === 1 ? [[0]] : [[0, 1], [1, 0]];
      for (const pk of perms) for (const dr of perms) {
        let pos = c.pos; let now = start; let move = 0; let wait = 0;
        for (const i of pk) { const o = os[i]; const d = tt(pos, o.rest); move += d; now += d; const p = Math.max(now, o.ready); wait += p - now; now = p; pos = o.rest; }
        const leave = now; const del: number[] = [];
        for (const i of dr) { const o = os[i]; const d = tt(pos, o.cust); move += d; now += d; del[i] = now; pos = o.cust; }
        const sum = os.reduce((s, o, i) => s + del[i] - o.placed, 0);
        if (!best || sum < best.sum) best = { sum, end: now, pos, move, wait, leave, del };
      }
      return best;
    }
    function commit(c: C, t: number, os: O[], st: S) {
      const r = trip(c, t, os);
      os.forEach((o, i) => { st.deliv += r.del[i] - o.placed; st.food += r.leave - o.ready; st.n++; });
      c.moving += r.move; c.wait += r.wait; c.free = r.end; c.pos = r.pos; st.end = Math.max(st.end, r.end);
    }
    function hungarian(a: number[][]): number[] { // needs rows <= columns; returns the column chosen for each row
      const n = a.length; const m = a[0].length; const INF = 1e12;
      const u = new Array(n + 1).fill(0); const v = new Array(m + 1).fill(0); const p = new Array(m + 1).fill(0); const way = new Array(m + 1).fill(0);
      for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
        p[0] = i; let j0 = 0; const minv = new Array(m + 1).fill(INF); const used = new Array(m + 1).fill(false);
        do {
          used[j0] = true; const i0 = p[j0]; let d = INF; let j1 = 0;
          for (let j = 1; j <= m; j++) if (!used[j]) { const cur = a[i0 - 1][j - 1] - u[i0] - v[j]; if (cur < minv[j]) { minv[j] = cur; way[j] = j0; } if (minv[j] < d) { d = minv[j]; j1 = j; } }
          for (let j = 0; j <= m; j++) { if (used[j]) { u[p[j]] += d; v[j] -= d; } else minv[j] -= d; }
          j0 = j1;
        } while (p[j0] !== 0);
        do { const j1 = way[j0]; p[j0] = p[j1]; j0 = j1; } while (j0);
      }
      const res = new Array(n).fill(-1); for (let j = 1; j <= m; j++) if (p[j]) res[p[j] - 1] = j - 1; return res;
    }
    type Pend = { o: O; since: number };
    function nearestIdle(couriers: C[], t: number, at: P): C | null {
      let best: C | null = null; let bd = FAR;
      for (const c of couriers) if (c.free <= t) { const d = dist(c.pos, at); if (d < bd) { bd = d; best = c; } }
      return best;
    }
    function run(strategy: string, world: { orders: O[]; couriers: C[] }, W: number) {
      const couriers: C[] = world.couriers.map((c) => ({ ...c })); const orders = world.orders; const st: S = { deliv: 0, food: 0, n: 0, end: 0 };
      let next = 0; let pending: Pend[] = [];
      for (let t = 0; t < HORIZON_MIN && st.n < orders.length; t++) {
        while (next < orders.length && orders[next].placed <= t) pending.push({ o: orders[next++], since: t });
        if (strategy === 'greedy') {
          pending = pending.filter((u) => { const c = nearestIdle(couriers, t, u.o.rest); if (!c) return true; commit(c, t, [u.o], st); return false; });
        } else if (strategy === 'batch') {
          const used = new Set<number>(); const units: { os: O[]; since: number }[] = [];
          for (let i = 0; i < pending.length; i++) {
            if (used.has(i)) continue; let bj = -1; let bd = FAR;
            for (let j = i + 1; j < pending.length; j++) {
              if (used.has(j)) continue; const a = pending[i].o; const b = pending[j].o; const dr = dist(a.rest, b.rest); const dc = dist(a.cust, b.cust);
              if (dr <= BATCH.restMax && dc <= BATCH.custMax && dr + dc < bd) { bd = dr + dc; bj = j; }
            }
            if (bj >= 0) { used.add(i); used.add(bj); units.push({ os: [pending[i].o, pending[bj].o], since: Math.min(pending[i].since, pending[bj].since) }); }
          }
          const waiting: Pend[] = [];
          pending.forEach((u, i) => { if (used.has(i)) return; if (t - u.since >= W) units.push({ os: [u.o], since: u.since }); else waiting.push(u); });
          units.sort((a, b) => a.since - b.since); const left: Pend[] = [];
          for (const u of units) { const c = nearestIdle(couriers, t, u.os[0].rest); if (!c) { u.os.forEach((o) => left.push({ o, since: u.since })); continue; } commit(c, t, u.os, st); }
          pending = [...waiting, ...left];
        } else if (t % W === 0) {
          const due = pending.filter((u) => u.o.ready - t <= W + LOOKAHEAD_MIN).sort((a, b) => a.o.ready - b.o.ready).slice(0, couriers.length);
          if (due.length) {
            const cost = due.map((u) => couriers.map((c) => {
              const avail = Math.max(c.free, t); if (avail > t + W) return UNAVAILABLE;
              const arr = avail + tt(c.pos, u.o.rest); const pk = Math.max(arr, u.o.ready);
              return (pk - u.o.ready) * WEIGHTS.foodWait + (pk - arr) + tt(c.pos, u.o.rest) * WEIGHTS.drive + (avail - t) * WEIGHTS.busy;
            }));
            const got = new Set<Pend>();
            hungarian(cost).forEach((j, i) => { if (j >= 0 && cost[i][j] < UNAVAILABLE) { commit(couriers[j], t, [due[i].o], st); got.add(due[i]); } });
            pending = pending.filter((u) => !got.has(u));
          }
        }
      }
      const horizon = Math.max(1, st.end); const n = Math.max(1, st.n);
      const move = couriers.reduce((s, c) => s + c.moving, 0); const wait = couriers.reduce((s, c) => s + c.wait, 0);
      return { n: st.n, deliv: st.deliv / n, food: st.food / n, util: move / (couriers.length * horizon), wait: wait / n, end: st.end };
    }
    //#sim-end
    // ---- page ----
    const NS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
    const map = q<SVGSVGElement>('[data-map]');
    const cell = MAP_PX / G;
    const mk = (tag: string, attrs: Record<string, string | number>) => { const e = document.createElementNS(NS, tag) as SVGElement; for (const k in attrs) { if (k === 'fill' || k === 'stroke') e.style.setProperty(k, String(attrs[k])); else e.setAttribute(k, String(attrs[k])); } return e; };
    function drawMap(w: { rests: P[]; orders: O[]; couriers: C[] }) {
      const parts: Element[] = [mk('rect', { x: 0, y: 0, width: MAP_PX, height: MAP_PX, fill: 'var(--surface-2)', stroke: 'var(--border)' })];
      w.orders.forEach((o) => parts.push(mk('circle', { cx: (o.cust.x + 0.5) * cell, cy: (o.cust.y + 0.5) * cell, r: 1.6, fill: 'var(--muted)', opacity: 0.55 })));
      w.rests.forEach((r) => parts.push(mk('rect', { x: r.x * cell + 1, y: r.y * cell + 1, width: cell - 2, height: cell - 2, fill: 'var(--accent)' })));
      w.couriers.forEach((c) => parts.push(mk('circle', { cx: (c.pos.x + 0.5) * cell, cy: (c.pos.y + 0.5) * cell, r: 3.4, fill: 'var(--good)', stroke: 'var(--bg)', 'stroke-width': 1 })));
      map.replaceChildren(...parts);
    }
    const names = ['Nearest courier', 'Two per courier', 'Window assignment'];
    function draw() {
      const no = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-o]').value); const nc = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-c]').value); const W = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-w]').value); const seed = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-seed]').value);
      q('[data-oval]').textContent = String(no); q('[data-cval]').textContent = String(nc); q('[data-wval]').textContent = String(W);
      const world = makeWorld(seed, no, nc); drawMap(world);
      const res = ['greedy', 'batch', 'window'].map((s) => run(s, world, W));
      const bestDeliv = Math.min(...res.map((r) => r.deliv)); const bestFood = Math.min(...res.map((r) => r.food));
      res.forEach((r, i) => {
        const k = i + 1;
        q(`[data-o${k}]`).textContent = `${r.deliv.toFixed(1)} min per order`;
        q(`[data-n${k}]`).textContent = `food waiting ${r.food.toFixed(1)} min, courier utilisation ${Math.round(r.util * 100)}%, couriers waiting at counters ${r.wait.toFixed(1)} min per order, last delivery at minute ${Math.round(r.end)}`;
        q<HTMLElement>(`[data-b${k}]`).style.setProperty('--c', r.deliv === bestDeliv ? 'var(--good)' : r.deliv > bestDeliv * WORSE_X ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--accent)');
      });
      const wi = res.findIndex((r) => r.deliv === bestDeliv); const g = res[0];
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); out.classList.toggle('bad', g.deliv > bestDeliv * WORSE_X);
      const foodBest = res.findIndex((r) => r.food === bestFood);
      out.textContent = `${names[wi]} gives the shortest delivery: ${bestDeliv.toFixed(1)} min, against ${g.deliv.toFixed(1)} min for nearest courier (${Math.round((1 - bestDeliv / g.deliv) * 100)}% less). ${foodBest === wi ? 'It also has the least food waiting' : `The least food waiting is with ${names[foodBest]}`} (${bestFood.toFixed(1)} min). ${nc >= PLENTIFUL * no ? 'Couriers are plentiful, so what matters is arriving when the food is ready.' : 'Couriers are scarce, so orders queue, and what matters is how much each courier trip carries.'}`;
    }
    let queued = false;
    const schedule = () => { if (!queued) { queued = true; requestAnimationFrame(() => { queued = false; draw(); }); } };
    root.addEventListener('input', schedule); root.addEventListener('change', schedule);
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .fd-map { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 280px; margin: 0.5rem auto; }
</style>
